\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.  At even, when the sun was set
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 The sick, O Lord, around Thee lay;
\par O in what divers pains they met
\par O with what joy they went away
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par    2.  Once more 'tis eventide, and we
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj Oppressed with various ills, draw near
\par What if Thy form we cannot see
\par We know and feel that Thou art here
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par    3. O Saviour Christ, our woes dispel
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 For some are sick, and some are sad
\par And some have never loved Thee well
\par And some have lost the love they had
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4.  And some are pressed with worldly care
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 And some are tried with sinful doubt
\par And some such grievous passions tear
\par That only Thou canst cast them out
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And some have found the world is vain
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Yet from the world they break not free
\par And some have friends who give them pain
\par Yet have not, sought a friend in Thee
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And none, O Lord, have perfect rest
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj For none are wholly free from sin
\par And they who fain would serve Thee best
\par Are conscious most of wrong within.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

